From ba3eca1ab720ed2e1355d6dffea3935eccd40566 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:28:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 54/54] world: share block states' property maps

Hypothesis: the block registry's 35,723 states each own a BTreeMap, and even a map with one entry takes a whole
node of over 500 bytes: 19 MiB, the largest single thing in the game's heap. Most of those maps are equal to
another state's: every stairs block has the same 80.

Change: BlockState.properties is Properties, a map behind an Arc that reads like the map and copies on write,
and BlockRegistry::from_states gives equal maps one allocation. Everything else that reads or edits a state's
properties compiles as it was.

Number: the game's heap at rest on an R36S, 292 to 271 MB.

Falsifier: a state's properties change when another state's are edited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
